# LawApp Handoff Auto-Generator

## When to trigger
Generate a handoff snapshot when ANY of these is true. Err on the side of
generating EARLY rather than missing it. Do not wait for an exact percentage,
because a live context figure may not be available to this rule.

- The user types any of: handoff, sync, recover, continue, checkpoint.
- Context usage is at or above 90% if that figure is visible.
- The session is long and has made major multi-step build progress.
- A major milestone just completed: a task finished, a build phase closed,
  a migration applied, or a service brought up.

If unsure whether the session is heavy, generate the snapshot anyway. A spare
snapshot costs nothing; a missed one loses the session.

## Behaviour when triggered (mandatory)
1. STOP current coding. Change no other code until the handoff is complete.
2. Read REAL state first: run `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`,
   `git rev-parse --short HEAD`, `git status`, and check running services and
   applied migrations. Never write state from memory.
3. Generate all five files under `docs/handoff/`, overwriting the previous set.
4. Make the five files consistent with each other.
5. Continue only if the user asks.

## Hard rules
- No guessing. Unknown value = `UNKNOWN - requires verification`. Never fabricate
  state, services, commits, or test results.
- Deterministic. Every value reflects real repo, service, and database state now.
- Fixed namespaces only: `lawapp-api`, `lawapp-rag`, `lawapp-ai`,
  `lawapp-security`, `lawapp-monitoring`. Never invent a namespace.
- Secrets: list names or status only, never values.
- Style: clean Markdown, short bullets, engineering-focused, no fluff,
  hyphens not em dashes.

## Files to generate

### docs/handoff/HANDOFF.md
Metadata block first:
```
Generated: <timestamp>
Repo: serverax/lawapp
Branch: <current branch>
Commit: <short hash>
Phase: <current phase 1-6>
```
Then: completed (bullets); recently modified; currently running (services,
pipelines, agents); broken or failing; build phase 01-06 and position in it;
RAG status (retrieval, embeddings, rules DB); agent status (orchestration,
reasoning, governance); legal compliance and guardrail status.

### docs/handoff/ARCHITECTURE_STATE.md
Frontend (UI, WASM); backend (API, orchestration); RAG (pgvector, embeddings,
ingestion); Graph RAG (status); database (tables, migrations, rules table);
security (encryption, GDPR, de-identification); Kubernetes / deployment.

### docs/handoff/DEPLOYMENT_STATE.md
Namespaces (fixed list only); services running; secrets configured (names only);
ingress status; pod status; health checks (API, DB, RAG, worker); failing
deployments or CrashLoopBackOffs.

### docs/handoff/NEXT_TASKS.md
Top 5 priority tasks (max 5); blocking issues; fixes required before next phase;
phase alignment (1-6); immediate next steps (actionable commands or tasks).

### docs/handoff/KNOWN_ISSUES.md
Open bugs; technical debt; failing tests; missing integrations; data ingestion
gaps; legal data verification issues; unstable pipeline components.
